@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "76 tracked files carried `/Users/<name>/...`: S3 score logs, which record the command each oracle ran. The command is the result; where the machine kept its files is not, and a public repository should not carry either the username or the layout." }
~ Take the home directory out of the published results and the docs

The command is the result; where the machine kept its files is not, and a public repository should not carry either the username or the layout.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "rust-version = \"1.86\"" }
~ Set MSRV to Rust 1.86

To ensure compatibility with dependencies that require newer versions of Rust.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-3 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "homepage     = \"https://github.com/vulogov/rust_smysl\"\nkeywords     = [\"cargo-subcommand\", \"rationale\", \"provenance\", \"smysl\", \"decisions\"]\ncategories   = [\"development-tools::cargo-plugins\", \"development-tools\"]" }
~ Add homepage, keywords, categories, and README to each crate

To provide necessary metadata for crates.io listing and discovery.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "crates.io resolves path dependencies by version, so git, facts and corpus go first, then bench and extract, then verdict and evidence, then the subcommand." }
~ Publish eight crates in a specific order

To ensure path dependencies are resolved correctly by crates.io.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo-smysl` keeps its own keywords rather than the workspace's: it is the crate people install, and they find it by searching for a cargo subcommand." }
~ Keep `cargo-smysl` keywords separate from the workspace

`cargo-smysl` is the crate people install, and they find it by searching for a cargo subcommand.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It also records what to be sure of before publishing, since a version can be yanked but never removed, and a crate name is claimed on first publish." }
~ Document the release process in `docs/releasing.md`

To provide clear instructions for maintaining and publishing the project.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Eight crates publish; the evaluation tooling does not, and says so." }
~ Exclude `cargo-smysl-eval` from publication

`cargo-smysl-eval` is evaluation tooling that reads files outside its own package.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Model-free and self-contained (plan §1): git objects are read with gix, never by running `git`." }
~ Use `gix` for reading git objects instead of running `git`

To ensure self-contained operation without relying on external binaries.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Label and adjudication files are TOML: a person edits them by hand, so they are not JSON." }
~ Pin dependencies to specific versions in the workspace

To maintain consistency across all crates in the workspace.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Hosted providers need TLS; the default build has no network stack at all (D18)." }
~ Add `hosted` feature to some crates for optional TLS support

To provide flexibility in network requirements.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Label and adjudication files are TOML: a person edits them by hand, so they are not JSON." }
~ Use `serde_json` and `toml` for configuration files

To support human-editable configuration files.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/1693fc23e399.smy@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A published package cannot reach outside itself, so the crate-level README is short and the full documentation stays in the repository." }
~ Include `README.md` in each crate for crates.io listing

To provide brief descriptions for each crate on crates.io.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The command is the result; where the machine kept its files is not, and a public repository should not carry either the username or the layout." }
~ Remove home directory paths from published results and documentation.

A public repository should not carry either the username or the layout, and the results themselves are worth keeping.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The paths are rewritten to `<repo>` and `~`, byte for byte otherwise, because the results themselves are worth keeping." }
~ Rewrite paths to `<repo>` and `~` in published results.

Paths are rewritten to `<repo>` and `~`, byte for byte otherwise, because the results themselves are worth keeping.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The harness now redacts as it writes, so a later run does not put them back." }
~ Redact home directory paths as the harness writes.

The harness now redacts as it writes, so a later run does not put them back.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": They say `<your repository>` and `~/.rustup/...` now. }
~ Update documentation to use `<your repository>` instead of `/Users/you/...`.

Two documents showed sample output with `/Users/you/...` in it, which taught the same bad habit to anyone copying the format; they say `<your repository>` and `~/.rustup/...` now.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": and quote 0.2.0 rather than a version that has moved on. }
~ Update documentation to quote version 0.2.0 instead of a version that has moved on.

Two documents showed sample output with `/Users/you/...` in it, which taught the same bad habit to anyone copying the format; they say `<your repository>` and `~/.rustup/...` now, and quote 0.2.0 rather than a version that has moved on.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A public repository should not carry either the username or the layout. }
~ Do not include the username in the published results.

A public repository should not carry either the username or the layout.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:2b514c5b163a1d9044f8a0ec08e97f41d8158711 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The remaining `/home/...` in the S3 patches are placeholders an agent wrote in test code (`/home/a-smysl-user`), not anybody's path." }
~ Keep the remaining `/home/...` in the S3 patches as placeholders.

The remaining `/home/...` in the S3 patches are placeholders an agent wrote in test code (`/home/a-smysl-user`), not anybody's path.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/cargo-smysl-install.md@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Deterministic commands are safe to gate on today, because they involve no model at all." }
~ Ensure deterministic commands do not involve a model.

Deterministic commands are safe to gate on today, because they involve no model at all.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/cargo-smysl-install.md@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The default, and the one to use. Every figure in the README comes from it." }
~ Use a local provider by default for `extract`, `check`, and `evidence` commands.

A local provider is free and the corpus shows it.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/cargo-smysl-install.md@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Twice the recall of the 14B and far less noise, about $2 per pass over 93 changes. Worth it when a judgement matters." }
~ Use a hosted provider for `check` when precision matters.

A hosted provider like DeepSeek is twice the recall of the 14B and far less noise, about $2 per pass over 93 changes. Worth it when a judgement matters.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/cargo-smysl-install.md@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "When the corpus must stay clean, use a hosted pro-class model." }
~ Use a hosted provider for `evidence` when the corpus must stay clean.

A hosted pro-class model is recommended for `evidence` when the corpus must stay clean.

@decision d/g2b514c5b163a-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/cargo-smysl-install.md@2b514c5b163a }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A 7B model on this task produces about ten findings per change, and `check` is already advisory at one-in-ten precision on the 14B." }
~ Do not use 7B and below models for `check`, as they over-produce decisions.

A 7B model on this task produces about ten findings per change, and `check` is already advisory at one-in-ten precision on the 14B.

